    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0490" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3419</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Group to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 20.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We received your letter of May 17th,<anchor
                        n="55" xml:id="d319-f1"/> enclosing a copy of a telegram from the Embassy at
                    Paris of May 14th,<anchor n="56" xml:id="d319-f2"/> transmitting a message from
                    Mr. Lamont regarding the proposed formation of a council to consider Consortium
                    matters.</p>
                <p>The American Group met today and discussed this proposal, and we transmit for
                    your information copy of a telegram which we are despatching to Mr.
                        Lamont,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d319-f3"/> indicating the approval of our
                    Group as therein set forth.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. P. Morgan</hi> &amp; Co.<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">For the American Group</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
